## Two independent failure mechanisms

**Shared parser:** for day-first tenant locales, the shared parser reads month first.
For example, entering 07/04/2026 intending 7 April is interpreted as 4 July.
The supplied classifier places app/email reports and booking-v2 form reports here.
Track the repair in [engineering issue #1](https://github.com/jarek-mazur-allegro/megadev/issues/1).

**booking-v3 hint:** this form prints MM/DD/YYYY even for day-first tenants, while
interpreting the input the tenant's way. Following the hint with 08/06/2026 intending
6 August instead produces 8 June. The relevant tenants are alder.physio (de-DE),
copper.studio (es-ES), and pale.harbour (pt-PT).
Track this separate repair in [engineering issue #2](https://github.com/jarek-mazur-allegro/megadev/issues/2).

These examples follow the supplied mechanisms; they are not results of running the
production booking service. The exported code is evidence for this classification,
not a production patch or an independent reproduction environment.

