## Proposed triage rule: compare causes, not subjects

Resolve the tenant, read its locale and booking-form version, and check the channel.
Classify with `causeOf`; merge only when `sameCause` confirms the same known cause.
Do not auto-merge an unknown tenant or an unplaced report. A subject is a search aid,
not the duplicate key.

- **Different subjects, same cause:** kettle.books app versus email belong together.
- **Same subject and tenant, different causes:** alder.physio form (booking-v3 hint)
  versus app (shared parser) must stay separate.
- **Same subject and channel, different tenants:** copper.studio form versus morrow.tax
  form must stay separate because their form versions differ.
- **Different subjects, same cause:** pale.harbour form and alder.physio form can merge.
- **Unknown tenant:** identical text alone does not establish a known shared cause.

The accepted [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) is historical evidence
and has not been edited. This review recommends replacing its subject-only policy
through a new decision; it does not claim the desk has already approved or deployed one.
The original [triage page](/kb/triage/dedupe) says to merge on subject, while its
`DedupeExplorer` runs cause-based checks. Read both the words and what the components do.

